# {{display}}

Scaffolded by `nmp init {{name}}`.

## Explicit Feature Composition (ADR-0069)

`crates/{{pkg}}` is a **thin composition shell** over reusable NMP framework
installers. Its `register` function installs the substrate floor explicitly,
then leaves selected protocol features and app-owned modules visible in this app
root. `crates/{{facade_pkg}}` is the app-owned UniFFI facade native shells link;
it owns the runtime by value and delegates lifecycle, dispatch, and capability
mechanics to `nmp-uniffi-support`. Production policy is not hidden behind a
preset or copied into native code.

## Starter contract

The generated app demonstrates the boring v1 path:

| Surface | Starter shape |
|------|------|
| Runtime | `examples/shell.rs` uses `nmp_native_runtime::NmpAppBuilder`, calls `{{crate_ident}}::register(&mut builder)` once, declares projection consumption, declares relay policy, then starts. Swift/Kotlin apps use `{{facade_struct}}` from `crates/{{facade_pkg}}`. |
| Timeline/read | `starter_home_feed_key()` + `starter_home_feed_spec()` declare this app's typed home-timeline read surface with `feed::events()` from `source::active_user().follows()`; `open_home_timeline_session()` opens it through `app.feeds().open_spec(...)` so platform shells render Rust/NMP projection output instead of owning subscription or cache policy. |
| Profile/content | Component hosts read `refs.profile`, authoritative `refs.event`, and derived `refs.event.envelopes`. Do not use pre-v1 whole-map projections. |
| Component host | Install one app-root provider such as SwiftUI `NmpComponentHost` or Compose `NmpComponentHostProvider`; leaf components render and manage visible claim/release only. |
| Compose/write | Platform shells build bytes with the app-local generated builder `GeneratedActionBuilders.addEntry(...)`, then pass those bytes to `{{facade_struct}}.dispatchAction(...)`. Shells do not spell action namespaces, arbitrary event kinds, or FlatBuffers payloads by hand. |
| Ownership | Product facts, routing, publish semantics, cache invalidation, and projection derivation stay in Rust/NMP. SwiftUI, Compose, web, or TUI shells render snapshots and execute capabilities only. |

## Layout

| Path | What |
|------|------|
| `nmp.toml` | NMP dependency policy (read by `nmp upgrade`). |
| `action-builders.json` | App-local typed action-builder contract for `{{name}}.entries.add`. |
| `generated/` | Swift/Kotlin/TypeScript action builders generated from `action-builders.json`. |
| `crates/{{pkg}}/src/lib.rs` | The composition shell: `register` → explicit substrate/protocol/app composition, plus an example app-owned domain (`EntryRecord`). **App nouns never go in `nmp-core`** (doctrine D0). |
| `crates/{{pkg}}/src/entry_action.rs` | The app-owned typed action module and `ActionPayload` decoder reached by generated builders. |
| `crates/{{pkg}}/src/entry_view.rs` | The app-owned reactive read model: declared dependencies, bounded state, event handlers, and snapshot shape. |
| `crates/{{facade_pkg}}/src/lib.rs` | The app-owned UniFFI facade: `setup_scaffolding!`, facade-local callbacks/records, and delegation to `nmp-uniffi-support`. |
| `ci/check-uniffi-bindings.sh` | Builds `crates/{{facade_pkg}}` and runs `uniffi-bindgen --library` for Swift/Kotlin bindings. |
| `crates/{{pkg}}/examples/shell.rs` | Headless shell: `NmpAppBuilder` → `register` → `start`. |

## Build and run

```sh
cargo check                              # core + app facade compile as-is
cargo test -p {{pkg}}                    # shell tests pass
cargo test -p {{facade_pkg}}             # facade tests pass
cargo run --manifest-path {{nmp_codegen_manifest}} -p nmp-codegen -- gen action-builders --registry action-builders.json --check
bash ci/check-uniffi-bindings.sh          # Swift/Kotlin facade bindings generate
cargo run --example shell -p {{pkg}}     # build → app-core register → start
```

## NMP dependency modes

The scaffold pins NMP one of two ways (see `crates/{{pkg}}/Cargo.toml`):

* **local checkout** (default / `nmp init … --nmp-path DIR`) — `path = …`
  dependencies into an NMP checkout, for framework development.
* **release** (`nmp init … --nmp-version X.Y.Z`) — git-rev pins on
  `github.com/pablof7z/nostr-multi-platform` at tag `vX.Y.Z`. External
  consumers pin NMP by git rev; see `docs/architecture/external-consumers.md`
  in the NMP repo.

## Upgrade NMP

```sh
nmp upgrade --to 0.4.0    # bump the pinned rev + rewrite nmp-* deps
```

## Next steps

1. Add your app-specific module registrations inside `register` in
   `crates/{{pkg}}/src/lib.rs`.
2. Replace the example `Entry` domain with your real nouns.
3. Install a component host with fixtures while wiring UI tests, for example
   `nmp add component swiftui/component-host --with fixture`.
4. Run `bash ci/check-uniffi-bindings.sh` and put the generated UniFFI bindings
   plus action builders in the host target that dispatches bytes.
5. Build a platform shell (SwiftUI / Compose / web / TUI) over the public
   binding for that platform: this app facade for native Swift/Kotlin,
   wasm-bindgen for browser Workers, or direct Rust for Rust-native shells.
6. Read the v1 runtime/component migration guide in the NMP checkout:
   `docs/migration.md`.
